---
// Public marketplace — for everyone, logged in or not (owner decision,
// SPEC-2026-09-01-LISTING-CONTENT-AND-BOOKING.md A1.1). It used to bounce a
// signed-in visitor into the dashboard-wrapped /dashboard/marketplace via
// <AuthRedirect/>; that redirect is now REMOVED on purpose. A logged-in user
// returns to their dashboard via the header's DASHBOARD button, not by being
// forced off this page. /dashboard/marketplace itself now just 301s here.
//
// [DEMO-MARKET-2 2026-08-29] RESTORED TO REAL DATA (owner decision).
//
// This route served the bazaar design comp from 2026-08-26 ([DEMO-MARKET-1]) — hardcoded
// mock cards that could not be searched, filtered or booked, with every card linking to
// the same demo listing. Real visitors were seeing fiction on the marketplace page the
// header, the footer and a dozen CTAs all point at.
//
// The trade the owner accepted: production currently has ZERO published listings
// (`/api/explore` returns `{"listings":[]}`), so this page shows MarketplaceBrowse's
// "Nothing here yet" empty state until listings exist. An honest empty marketplace beats
// a convincing fake one — a visitor who books nothing is better than a visitor who tries
// to book a listing that does not exist.
//
// MarketplaceBrowse was never deleted and has been live at /dashboard/marketplace the
// whole time, so this is a straight restore, not a rebuild. The comp itself also still
// exists in web/src/generated/ and is still served at /[username]/[slug].
//
// [MARKET-BAZAAR-1 2026-08-31] The BAZAAR LOOK IS BACK — the mock data is not, and
// must not come back with it. The owner asked for the comp's design on this route
// again, so the hero, the truck-art category tiles and the section chrome are now real
// components (BazaarHero.astro, TruckBorder.astro, MarketplaceBrowse.astro) sitting on
// top of the same /api/explore reads this route has used since [DEMO-MARKET-2].
//
// The distinction that makes this safe is the one [DEMO-MARKET-2] was about: the comp's
// LAYOUT was never the problem, its DATA was. So the design is copied and the numbers
// are not — no "2,400 CREATORS LIVE" eyebrow, no per-tile "8 LISTINGS", no invented
// ratings or followings on the cards (see chipsFor in ListingTile.tsx), and every card
// links to its own real listing. With zero published listings in production, this page
// still lands on an empty state; it is now a bazaar-styled one (ExploreGrid) rather
// than a plain box. If you are about to add a placeholder card "just so it looks full",
// that is the exact change that got reverted on 2026-08-29.
export const prerender = false;

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import MarketplaceBrowse from '../components/MarketplaceBrowse.astro';

// [MKT-3GROUP-WEB-1 2026-09-05] ?group= replaces ?vertical= (which replaced
// ?category= and ?kind=). The page's taxonomy is now the THREE marketplace
// groups (web/src/lib/marketGroups.ts, over lib/listingTaxonomy.ts), which is
// what both the tiles and the filter rail speak.
const group = Astro.url.searchParams.get('group') ?? Astro.url.searchParams.get('vertical') ?? undefined;
// [MARKET-BAZAAR-1] ?q= is set by the bazaar search strip, which is a plain GET
// form so a search is a real, shareable URL. ExploreGrid seeds itself from it.
const q = Astro.url.searchParams.get('q')?.trim() || undefined;

Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'public, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=300');
---

<Base
  title="Marketplace · avatok.ai"
  description="Browse live streams, 1:1 sessions, events and AI agents from creators worldwide — no app required."
>
  {/* [MARKET-BAZAAR-1] No max-width and no padding here: the bazaar hero is a
      full-bleed terracotta band with a truck-art strip that has to reach both
      edges of the viewport. MarketplaceBrowse owns the gutters for everything
      below the band (its `gutters` const), so wrapping it in a max-w-6xl
      container would both crop the band and double-indent the grid. */}
  <main>
    <MarketplaceBrowse hrefBase="" group={group} q={q} showHero={true} showSplit={true} />
  </main>
</Base>
